---
// What the site stores on a visitor's device, and why none of it needs
// their consent. Linked from the footer.
import Layout from '../layout/Layout.astro';

import '../styles/global.css';

const CLOUDFLARE_COOKIES =
	'https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/reference/policies-compliances/cloudflare-cookies/';
const link =
	'font-semibold text-accent underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink focus-visible:ring-4 focus-visible:ring-accent/50 focus-visible:outline-none';
---

<Layout
	title="Cookies · Elliot Lewis"
	description="The one cookie elliotleelewis.com's host may set, what the game remembers, and why none of it needs your consent."
	path="/cookies"
>
	<main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-24">
		<p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.25em] text-accent uppercase">
			Privacy
		</p>
		<h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-7xl">
			Cookies<span class="text-accent">.</span>
		</h1>
		<p class="mt-6 text-lg/relaxed text-ink/85">
			This site doesn’t set any cookies of its own, and nothing on it
			tracks you. The only cookie you might get comes from Cloudflare,
			which hosts the site, and only to keep it secure. That’s why there’s
			no banner: nothing here needs your consent.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-3xl font-semibold">
			Cloudflare’s security cookie
		</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink/85">
			When Cloudflare’s bot protection can’t tell whether a visit comes
			from a person, it asks your browser to pass a quick check. This
			cookie remembers that you passed, so you aren’t checked again on
			every page.
		</p>
		<dl class="mt-6 grid gap-x-6 gap-y-3 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-5 sm:grid-cols-[auto_1fr]">
			<dt class="font-semibold">Name</dt>
			<dd class="font-mono text-sm">cf_clearance</dd>
			<dt class="font-semibold">Set by</dt>
			<dd>Cloudflare, only if you’re asked to pass a check</dd>
			<dt class="font-semibold">Purpose</dt>
			<dd>
				Security: telling people from bots. It isn’t used to identify or
				follow you.
			</dd>
			<dt class="font-semibold">Kept for</dt>
			<dd>As long as the check lasts, 30 minutes by default</dd>
			<dt class="font-semibold">Consent</dt>
			<dd>
				Not needed. It’s strictly necessary to keep the site secure,
				which the ePrivacy Directive and the UK’s PECR exempt.
			</dd>
		</dl>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink/85">
			<a href={CLOUDFLARE_COOKIES} class={link}>
				Cloudflare’s own list
			</a>{' '}
			explains it in more detail.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-3xl font-semibold">
			What the game remembers
		</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink/85">
			The game keeps your best score and the easter eggs you’ve found in
			your browser’s local storage, as{' '}
			<code class="font-mono text-sm">hero-best-trees</code> and{' '}
			<code class="font-mono text-sm">hero-easter-egg-hits</code>, so
			they’re still there next time you play. They never leave your
			device, and clearing your browser’s data for this site removes them.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-3xl font-semibold">Analytics</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink/85">
			I count visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which sets no cookies,
			stores nothing on your device and doesn’t fingerprint you.
		</p>

		<p class="mt-12">
			<a
				href="/"
				class="inline-block rounded-full bg-ink px-5 py-2.5 font-semibold text-paper hover:bg-ink/85 focus-visible:ring-4 focus-visible:ring-accent/50 focus-visible:outline-none"
			>
				Back to the trailhead
			</a>
		</p>
	</main>
</Layout>
